{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## STOP + ESCALATION — this bug is ALREADY FIXED and MERGED; my change would REVERT it\n\nWhile waiting on CI for my Gerrit change 2352, a parallel session working this same ticket posted a heads-up. I verified its claims independently against origin/main. Summary of what I found:\n\n**The fix already landed.** `c68cc1de3185` (\"Resolve the sweep's code root, not compose it\", Gerrit 2344) is an ancestor of current `origin/main` (`565e1856bc9d`). On origin/main `run_sweep` already reads `repo_root = _cfg.repo_root_or_none()` (line ~233), the `# repo-root-ok:` sanction is already removed, and the four `run_sweep` tests + the guard self-test are already present. It merged with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n\n**My worktree base was stale.** This worktree was branched from `ae203145`, which PREDATES the 2344 merge, so the buggy `dirname(tracker)` still appeared here and I implemented against it. The approved-plan premise (\"the ONE site auspicial deliberately deferred\", unfixed) is no longer true.\n\n**My change (2352) is worse AND would revert the merged fix.** It replaces `repo_root_or_none()` with `compaction_child_repo_root(StorePaths(tracker).canonical)`. Because `main` is Rebase-If-Necessary, submitting it would land that replacement on top of the merge — reverting it. And the operator-approved `dirname(canonical tracker)` fallback is measurably narrower. Hard measurement I ran (relocated store, NO symlink, `REBAR_ROOT` UNSET, cwd inside the checkout — the inline `maybe_compact(trigger=\"always\")` case):\n\n- `dirname(canonical tracker)` → the external store's PARENT (`/…/elsewhere`) = the ORIGINAL BUG.\n- `repo_root_or_none()` → the checkout = CORRECT.\n\nThe merged design is correct when EITHER `REBAR_ROOT` is set OR cwd is in the checkout; `dirname(canonical tracker)` needs the store to be a symlink co-located with the checkout, a strictly narrower envelope. My in-worktree AC#4 test passed only because it used a co-located SYMLINK store, not this relocated-no-symlink case.\n\n**Actions I took (safe, reversible; no force, no destructive ops):**\n- Set Gerrit 2352 to **WIP** so no session can submit it.\n- Did **NOT** submit, **NOT** abandon, **NOT** close this ticket.\n- Left the earlier description edit in place; note it now mandates `compaction_child_repo_root`, which exists nowhere on origin/main — it reflects the approved-but-now-superseded plan, pending operator direction.\n\n**Why I am escalating rather than proceeding:** resolving this requires a design decision beyond the approved scope — e.g. (a) accept the merged `repo_root_or_none()` design, abandon 2352, and close this ticket against `c68cc1de3185`; or (b) rework 2352 as a refactor ON TOP of the merge if the resolver still wins on evidence (it does not, per the measurement above). Both are operator calls. The approved instruction was to *implement* `dirname(canonical tracker)`; reality diverged.\n\n**Related follow-ups filed by the parallel session (for context):** feisty-intense-mandrill `9058-0b67-4c6a-49c4` (the config-root guard does not flag `dirname(StorePaths(tracker).canonical)`, so that construct would sit unsanctioned); arty-larval-titmouse `a027-d86c-8a00-407c` (the merged in-repo AC#4 test survives the `repo_root=None` mutant, so the fallback arm is currently unasserted)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787959625428855001,"uuid":"cfbbff6e-715e-4c56-b5c2-beeaef64ea7d"}